Experiment No. 4 – Wireshark: Network Traffic Analysis

Date: 17/09/2026

Aim: To install Wireshark, capture network traffic and identify different protocols and data types.

Tools Required: Wireshark, computer and network connection.

Theory:

Wireshark is a network protocol analyzer used to capture and analyze network packets. It helps identify protocols, source and destination addresses, and protocol data.

Procedure:

Install and open Wireshark.
Select the active network interface (Wi-Fi/Ethernet).
Start capturing network traffic.
Generate network activity by browsing websites.
Stop the capture and examine packet details.
Identify protocols such as TCP, UDP, DNS and ICMP.

Packet Analysis:

TCP: Ensures reliable data transmission.
DNS: Converts domain names into IP addresses.
ICMP: Used for network diagnostics and error reporting.

Types of Data Observed:

Control Data: Connection establishment and management.
Addressing Data: Source and destination MAC/IP addresses.
Application Data: Data exchanged by applications.
Protocol Information: TCP, UDP, DNS and ICMP headers.

Result:

Wireshark was successfully used to capture and analyze network traffic. Different protocols, packets and data types were identified.
